LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
SUMMARY:Curator-led Tour
DESCRIPTION:Reserve your spot today for a rare opportunity to explore thi
 s amazing photographic collection in depth\, guided by the scholar who cu
 rated the exhibition. Read Ben Levy's bio. (https://artmuseum.indiana.edu
 /about/staff/_curatorial/levy-benjamin.html)  About the exhibition  Spann
 ing more than 150 years\, The Photographic Reflex celebrates a transforma
 tive gift to the Eskenazi Museum of Art at Indiana University: more than 
 one hundred works by eighty artists\, generously donated by Lee Marks and
  John C. DePrez Jr. This exhibition features photographs dating from 1856
  to 2017 and highlights the medium's extraordinary range\, both as a tool
  for documentation and as a vehicle for artistic exploration.  Photograph
 s dating from 1856 to 2017 reveal photography's dual role as both a tool 
 for documentation and a vehicle for artistic exploration. Organized into 
 five thematic sections—Play of Light\, Industrial Eye\, Photographic Fi
 gure\, Witness to Conflict\, and Impressed by Nature's Hand—the exhibit
 ion examines how photographers across disciplines have communicated ideas
 \, recorded history\, and shaped visual culture.  The exhibition includes
  works by many of the most influential figures in the medium\, from Beren
 ice Abbott\, Alfred Stieglitz\, Edward Steichen\, and Henri Cartier-Bress
 on to contemporary artists such as Edward Burtynsky\, Abelardo Morell\, S
 usan Derges\, and Vik Muniz.Read more about this exhibition. (https://art
 museum.indiana.edu/exhibitions/2026-08-29-photographic-reflex-marks-depre
 z.html)  &#160\;Know Before You GoSpace is limited to 15 participants. RS
 VP to reserve a space. Walk-ins are welcome if space is available. If thi
 s page says "registration has closed"\, this means that registration and 
 the waitlist have filled for this date and time.Plan to arrive early to c
 heck in. At 1:25 p.m.\, any unclaimed spaces may be released to guests wh
 o are standing by waiting for a space.Admission and tours are free.A smal
 l handbag may be carried at your side. Larger bags and backpacks will nee
 d to be stored before touring.Read about where to find us\, where to park
 \, accessibility\, and museum guidelines.When You ArriveCheck in with Gue
 st Services staff on the first floor.If you park in the IMU parking lot\,
  Guest Services can validate your parking voucher for a discount.Store ba
 ckpacks and large bags before touring. Lockers and coat racks are availab
 le.Keep space (18") between yourself\, including anything you're carrying
 \, and the art.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Reserve your spot today for a rare oppo
