SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: Totems and Traditions
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by artworks in the galleries\, students will explore
  how meaning can be built through design and structure. Join us to create
  your own mini slot sculpture pillar that celebrates the people\, traditi
 ons\, and values that make up who you are!  Program designed by our licen
 sed art educator for students in grades K-12.Know Before You Go:  Meet us
  in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the museum at 1 
 pm. Together\, we'll drop off personal items before exploring the galleri
 es.&#160\; After seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll he
 ad back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpie
 ces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Strollers are welcome. Chaperone 
 required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adult for ever
 y 6 children.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Inspired by artworks in the galleries\,
  students will explore how meaning can be built through design and struct
 ure. Join us to create your own mini slot sculpture pillar that celebrate
 s the people\, traditions\, and values that make up who you are!</p><p>  
 Program designed by our licensed art educator for students in grades K-12
 .</p><p><strong>Know Before You Go:</strong></p><p>  Meet us in the Simps
 on Center for Education on the 2nd floor of the museum at 1 pm. Together\
 , we'll drop off personal items before exploring the galleries.&#160\; Af
 ter seeing artworks that will inspire our project\, we'll head back to th
 e Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create our own masterpieces! Don't fo
 rget to dress for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers are welcome. <strong>Chaperon
 e required.</strong> We ask that chaperones be 18 or older\, with one adu
 lt for every 6 children.</p>
