DTSTART:20261008T170000Z
DTEND:20261008T190000Z
LOCATION:SIDNEY AND LOIS ESKENAZI MUSEUM OF ART
GEO:39.169144;-86.519739
SUMMARY:Homeschool Day: Cloth and Culture
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by Indonesian fabrics made by women\, students will 
 discover how cloth can tell stories about culture\, creativity\, and chan
 ge over time. Through printmaking techniques\, we'll experiment with repe
 tition and design to create our own patterned handkerchiefs. Join us to e
 xplore textile traditions and craft a one-of-a-kind piece inspired by glo
 bal artistry!  Program designed by our licensed art educator for students
  in grades K-12.Know Before You Go:  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Ed
 ucation on the 2nd floor of the museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off
  personal items before exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks tha
 t will inspire our project\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Maki
 ng Studio to create our own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mes
 s!  Strollers are welcome. Chaperone required. We ask that chaperones be 
 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 children.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Inspired by Indonesian fabrics made by 
 women\, students will discover how cloth can tell stories about culture\,
  creativity\, and change over time. Through printmaking techniques\, we'l
 l experiment with repetition and design to create our own patterned handk
 erchiefs. Join us to explore textile traditions and craft a one-of-a-kind
  piece inspired by global artistry!</p><p>  Program designed by our licen
 sed art educator for students in grades K-12.</p><p><strong>Know Before Y
 ou Go:</strong></p><p>  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on th
 e 2nd floor of the museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off personal ite
 ms before exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspir
 e our project\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to 
 create our own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!</p><p>  St
 rollers are welcome. <strong>Chaperone required.</strong> We ask that cha
 perones be 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 children.</p>
UID:20261008T170000Z-2344744@events.iu.edu
