 s K-12.Know Before You Go:  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education o
 n the 2nd floor of the museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off personal
  items before exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks that will in
 spire our project\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio
  to create our own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!  Strol
 lers are welcome. Chaperone required. We ask that chaperones be 18 or old
 er\, with one adult for every 6 children.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Students will look closely at still lif
 e paintings in the galleries\, discovering how artists use symbolism and 
 lighting to communicate mood and reveal more than meets the eye. After fi
 nding inspiration in the galleries\, students will create their own still
  life paintings by arranging and observing objects at their table to tell
  their own unique stories!</p><p>  Program designed by our licensed art e
 ducator for students in grades K-12.</p><p><strong>Know Before You Go:</s
 trong></p><p>  Meet us in the Simpson Center for Education on the 2nd flo
 or of the museum at 1 pm. Together\, we'll drop off personal items before
  exploring the galleries. After seeing artworks that will inspire our pro
 ject\, we'll head back to the Roehm Family Art-Making Studio to create ou
 r own masterpieces! Don't forget to dress for a mess!</p><p>  Strollers a
 re welcome. <strong>Chaperone required.</strong> We ask that chaperones b
 e 18 or older\, with one adult for every 6 children.</p>
